Let the virt board's high PCI MMIO window be smaller than 512 GiB.

The window is 512 GiB by default and has to fit under the guest physical
address size. Hypervisor.framework on an Apple M1 gives the guest 36 bits,
64 GiB, so QEMU drops the window without a word and every 64-bit BAR lands in
the 32-bit window at 0x10000000-0x3efeffff. A BAR is aligned to its size, so
the largest virtio-gpu host-visible window that fits there is 256 MiB, and
venus runs out of it with a few windows open.

Two things keep it out. `highmem-mmio-size` exists to change the window's
size but refuses anything below the default, and the high IO regions never
start below 256 GiB, past the end of a 36-bit space whatever their size. With
the check gone, and the 256 GiB floor kept only where the PA space reaches past
it, `highmem-mmio-size=16G` puts the window at 16 GiB, under the 64 GiB limit,
and the hostmem BAR can be as large as the guest wants. A host with more than
38 bits keeps the layout it had.

--- a/hw/arm/virt.c
+++ b/hw/arm/virt.c
@@ -1891,7 +1891,13 @@
         error_report("maxmem/slots too huge");
         exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
     }
-    if (base < vms->memmap[VIRT_MEM].base + LEGACY_RAMLIMIT_BYTES) {
+    /*
+     * A PA space that ends at or below the legacy limit has no room above
+     * it: the high IO regions go straight after the memory instead, or not
+     * at all.
+     */
+    if (base < vms->memmap[VIRT_MEM].base + LEGACY_RAMLIMIT_BYTES &&
+        BIT_ULL(pa_bits) > vms->memmap[VIRT_MEM].base + LEGACY_RAMLIMIT_BYTES) {
         base = vms->memmap[VIRT_MEM].base + LEGACY_RAMLIMIT_BYTES;
     }
 
@@ -2582,14 +2588,6 @@
 
     if (!is_power_of_2(size)) {
         error_setg(errp, "highmem-mmio-size is not a power of 2");
-        return;
-    }
-
-    if (size < DEFAULT_HIGH_PCIE_MMIO_SIZE) {
-        char *sz = size_to_str(DEFAULT_HIGH_PCIE_MMIO_SIZE);
-        error_setg(errp, "highmem-mmio-size cannot be set to a lower value "
-                         "than the default (%s)", sz);
-        g_free(sz);
         return;
     }
 
